Now I have all the information needed. Let me put together the full implementation plan.

---

## Implementation Plan: Connection Status Toast Notifications

### Executive Summary

Add a lightweight toast notification system that fires when the WebSocket connection drops ("Connection lost") and when it restores ("Reconnected"). The toast should not fire on the initial page load -- only on transitions after the first successful connection.

### Key Design Decisions

**1. Sonner vs. Radix Toast vs. Custom**

The `radix-ui` package (already installed) exports a full `Toast` primitive set (`Toast.Provider`, `Toast.Root`, `Toast.Title`, `Toast.Viewport`, etc.). This means we can build a shadcn/ui-style toast component **without installing any new dependency**. This is the recommended approach because:

- Zero new dependencies. Sonner would add ~14kB to the bundle.
- The `radix-ui` package already ships `@radix-ui/react-toast` as part of its bundle (confirmed in the lockfile and via runtime check).
- shadcn/ui's own `toast` component (distinct from their `sonner` component) is built on exactly this Radix primitive. We can follow that pattern directly.
- The usage here is extremely narrow (two possible toast messages, no complex queue), so sonner's full feature set is unnecessary overhead.

If sonner is still strongly preferred despite the extra dependency, I provide that as an alternative path at the end.

**2. Where the toast trigger logic lives**

The trigger logic should live in `app/dashboard/page.tsx` as a `useEffect` watching the `connected` boolean from `useWebSocket()`. Reasons:

- The `useWebSocket` hook is a pure data hook -- it manages WS state and returns it. Adding side effects like toast calls would break its single responsibility.
- The dashboard page already destructures `connected` and is the natural composition root.
- A `useEffect` in the page with a `hasConnectedRef` guard is the cleanest way to skip the initial load toast.

**3. Preventing the initial-load toast**

Use a `useRef<boolean>` called `hasConnectedRef`. On the first transition of `connected` to `true`, set the ref to `true` but do NOT fire a toast. On subsequent transitions, fire the appropriate toast. This ensures:
- Initial page load (connected goes `false` -> `true`): no toast.
- Connection drop (`true` -> `false`): shows "Connection lost".
- Reconnect (`false` -> `true`, after first connection): shows "Reconnected".

**4. Where the Toaster/Provider lives**

The `Toast.Provider` and `Toast.Viewport` should be placed in `app/layout.tsx`. This keeps them available app-wide (future-proofing for other toast uses) and follows the standard shadcn/ui placement pattern. However, since the root layout is a Server Component and the Toast provider is a client component, the provider needs to be wrapped in a `"use client"` component.

Since only the dashboard currently needs toasts, a pragmatic alternative is placing it directly inside `app/dashboard/page.tsx`. Given that this project has exactly one main page (the dashboard), either approach works. I recommend the dashboard page for now to keep `layout.tsx` minimal, with a note that it can be lifted to the layout when other pages need toasts.

**5. Visual design**

The toast should match the existing dark-first monospace aesthetic:
- Background: `oklch(0.16 0 0)` (same as `--card`)
- Border: `oklch(1 0 0 / 8%)` (same as `--border`)
- Font: monospace (inherited from body)
- Size: small, positioned bottom-right
- Icons: Lucide `WifiOff` (red-tinted) for disconnect, `Wifi` (green-tinted) for reconnect
- Auto-dismiss: 4 seconds
- Subtle slide-in animation (Radix Toast provides this by default)

---

### Step-by-Step Implementation

#### Step 1: Create the Toast UI component

**File: `/Users/chiu.fyi/thos/components/ui/toast.tsx`** (new file)

Build a shadcn/ui-style wrapper around Radix Toast primitives. This follows the exact same pattern as `components/ui/button.tsx` -- thin styled wrappers using `cn()` and `cva()`.

```tsx
"use client";

import * as React from "react";
import { Toast } from "radix-ui";
import { cva, type VariantProps } from "class-variance-authority";
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";
import { X } from "lucide-react";

const ToastProvider = Toast.Provider;
const ToastViewport = React.forwardRef<
  React.ComponentRef<typeof Toast.Viewport>,
  React.ComponentPropsWithoutRef<typeof Toast.Viewport>
>(({ className, ...props }, ref) => (
  <Toast.Viewport
    ref={ref}
    className={cn(
      "fixed bottom-0 right-0 z-[100] flex max-h-screen w-full flex-col-reverse p-4 sm:max-w-[360px]",
      className
    )}
    {...props}
  />
));
ToastViewport.displayName = "ToastViewport";

const toastVariants = cva(
  "group pointer-events-auto relative flex w-full items-center gap-3 overflow-hidden rounded-md border px-4 py-3 shadow-lg transition-all data-[swipe=cancel]:translate-x-0 data-[swipe=end]:translate-x-[var(--radix-toast-swipe-end-x)] data-[swipe=move]:translate-x-[var(--radix-toast-swipe-move-x)] data-[state=open]:animate-in data-[state=closed]:animate-out data-[swipe=end]:animate-out data-[state=closed]:fade-out-80 data-[state=closed]:slide-out-to-right-full data-[state=open]:slide-in-from-bottom-full",
  {
    variants: {
      variant: {
        default: "border bg-card text-card-foreground",
        destructive: "border-destructive/50 bg-destructive text-white",
      },
    },
    defaultVariants: { variant: "default" },
  }
);

const ToastRoot = React.forwardRef<
  React.ComponentRef<typeof Toast.Root>,
  React.ComponentPropsWithoutRef<typeof Toast.Root> &
    VariantProps<typeof toastVariants>
>(({ className, variant, ...props }, ref) => (
  <Toast.Root
    ref={ref}
    className={cn(toastVariants({ variant }), className)}
    {...props}
  />
));
ToastRoot.displayName = "ToastRoot";

const ToastClose = React.forwardRef<
  React.ComponentRef<typeof Toast.Close>,
  React.ComponentPropsWithoutRef<typeof Toast.Close>
>(({ className, ...props }, ref) => (
  <Toast.Close
    ref={ref}
    className={cn(
      "absolute right-2 top-2 rounded-sm opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-70 hover:!opacity-100",
      className
    )}
    {...props}
  >
    <X className="size-3.5" />
  </Toast.Close>
));
ToastClose.displayName = "ToastClose";

const ToastTitle = React.forwardRef<
  React.ComponentRef<typeof Toast.Title>,
  React.ComponentPropsWithoutRef<typeof Toast.Title>
>(({ className, ...props }, ref) => (
  <Toast.Title
    ref={ref}
    className={cn("text-xs font-medium", className)}
    {...props}
  />
));
ToastTitle.displayName = "ToastTitle";

const ToastDescription = React.forwardRef<
  React.ComponentRef<typeof Toast.Description>,
  React.ComponentPropsWithoutRef<typeof Toast.Description>
>(({ className, ...props }, ref) => (
  <Toast.Description
    ref={ref}
    className={cn("text-xs text-muted-foreground", className)}
    {...props}
  />
));
ToastDescription.displayName = "ToastDescription";

export {
  ToastProvider,
  ToastViewport,
  ToastRoot,
  ToastClose,
  ToastTitle,
  ToastDescription,
};
```

Key notes:
- Imports `Toast` from `"radix-ui"` (the same pattern as `button.tsx` importing `Slot` from `"radix-ui"`).
- Uses `text-xs` and monospace (inherited) for minimal visual footprint.
- The `tw-animate-css` package already installed provides `animate-in`, `animate-out`, `slide-in-from-bottom-full`, etc.

#### Step 2: Create a useToast hook for imperative toasting

**File: `/Users/chiu.fyi/thos/hooks/use-toast.ts`** (new file)

A minimal state hook that manages a queue of toasts. This follows the standard shadcn/ui `use-toast` pattern but stripped to the bare minimum needed.

```tsx
"use client";

import { useState, useCallback } from "react";

export interface ToastData {
  id: string;
  title: string;
  description?: string;
  variant?: "default" | "destructive";
  duration?: number;
  icon?: React.ReactNode;
}

let toastCounter = 0;

export function useToast() {
  const [toasts, setToasts] = useState<ToastData[]>([]);

  const toast = useCallback((data: Omit<ToastData, "id">) => {
    const id = `toast-${++toastCounter}`;
    setToasts((prev) => [...prev, { ...data, id }]);
  }, []);

  const dismiss = useCallback((id: string) => {
    setToasts((prev) => prev.filter((t) => t.id !== id));
  }, []);

  return { toasts, toast, dismiss };
}
```

#### Step 3: Create a Toaster component

**File: `/Users/chiu.fyi/thos/components/ui/toaster.tsx`** (new file)

This renders the toast list using the Radix primitives from Step 1.

```tsx
"use client";

import {
  ToastProvider,
  ToastViewport,
  ToastRoot,
  ToastClose,
  ToastTitle,
  ToastDescription,
} from "@/components/ui/toast";
import type { ToastData } from "@/hooks/use-toast";

export function Toaster({
  toasts,
  onDismiss,
}: {
  toasts: ToastData[];
  onDismiss: (id: string) => void;
}) {
  return (
    <ToastProvider swipeDirection="right">
      {toasts.map((t) => (
        <ToastRoot
          key={t.id}
          variant={t.variant}
          duration={t.duration ?? 4000}
          onOpenChange={(open) => {
            if (!open) onDismiss(t.id);
          }}
        >
          <div className="flex items-center gap-2.5">
            {t.icon}
            <div>
              <ToastTitle>{t.title}</ToastTitle>
              {t.description && (
                <ToastDescription>{t.description}</ToastDescription>
              )}
            </div>
          </div>
          <ToastClose />
        </ToastRoot>
      ))}
      <ToastViewport />
    </ToastProvider>
  );
}
```

#### Step 4: Wire up connection toasts in the dashboard page

**File: `/Users/chiu.fyi/thos/app/dashboard/page.tsx`** (modify)

Add the toast trigger logic via `useEffect` and render the `Toaster` component.

Changes:
1. Import `useToast` and `Toaster`.
2. Import `Wifi` and `WifiOff` from `lucide-react`.
3. Add a `hasConnectedRef` to track whether the first connection has occurred.
4. Add a `useEffect` that watches `connected` and fires toasts on state transitions (skipping the initial connect).
5. Render `<Toaster>` at the bottom of the JSX tree.

```tsx
// New imports to add:
import { useRef } from "react"; // already imported via useState
import { useToast } from "@/hooks/use-toast";
import { Toaster } from "@/components/ui/toaster";
import { Wifi, WifiOff } from "lucide-react";

// Inside DashboardPage():
const { toasts, toast, dismiss } = useToast();
const hasConnectedRef = useRef(false);

useEffect(() => {
  if (connected) {
    if (hasConnectedRef.current) {
      // This is a reconnection (not the first connect)
      toast({
        title: "Reconnected",
        description: "WebSocket connection restored",
        icon: <Wifi className="size-4 text-green-500 shrink-0" />,
        duration: 3000,
      });
    }
    hasConnectedRef.current = true;
  } else if (hasConnectedRef.current) {
    // Was connected, now disconnected
    toast({
      title: "Connection lost",
      description: "Attempting to reconnect...",
      icon: <WifiOff className="size-4 text-red-500 shrink-0" />,
      duration: 4000,
    });
  }
}, [connected, toast]);

// At the bottom of the JSX, after the closing </div> of the main layout
// but still inside the outermost fragment/wrapper:
<Toaster toasts={toasts} onDismiss={dismiss} />
```

The full return JSX becomes:

```tsx
return (
  <>
    <div className="relative flex h-dvh overflow-hidden">
      {/* ... existing sidebar, chat, tasks ... */}
    </div>
    <Toaster toasts={toasts} onDismiss={dismiss} />
  </>
);
```

#### Step 5: Update CHANGELOG.md

Per the project conventions ("All changes must be documented in CHANGELOG.md"), add an entry:

```markdown
